From aa4307fff1a6055fc30eb791e5d46df80a5112df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nyasha <nmushambi@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 11:02:41 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 11/13] Bluetooth: hci_bcm: power the chip before the serdev
 port opens

The flounder Broadcom chip must be powered before serdev opens the UART:
the port otherwise sees the unpowered chip's TX held low and only one reply
gets through.  Power it from the driver's probe path.

Signed-off-by: nyasha <nmushambi@proton.me>
---
 drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c
index 9286a5f40..2f63e521b 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c
@@ -1543,6 +1543,14 @@ static int bcm_serdev_probe(struct serdev_device *serdev)
 	if (err)
 		dev_err(&serdev->dev, "Failed to power down\n");
 
+	/* The flounder chip must be powered before serdev opens the UART:
+	 * the port otherwise sees the unpowered chip's TX held low and only
+	 * one reply gets through.
+	 */
+	err = bcm_gpio_set_power(bcmdev, true);
+	if (err)
+		dev_err(&serdev->dev, "Failed to power up\n");
+
 	data = device_get_match_data(bcmdev->dev);
 	if (data) {
 		bcmdev->max_autobaud_speed = data->max_autobaud_speed;
-- 
